{% doc %}
  ONE place that decides what the storefront says about stock. Every surface
  (product page, collection card, search results) captures this snippet and
  splits the result, so the wording can never drift between pages again.

  Output (one line, '|' separated, nothing else):
    kind|state|text|lead
      kind  = own | supplier | out
      state = exact | bucket | low | call | plain | out   (internal: staff,
              cart and call-to-book logic read it; customers never see it)
      text  = the customer-facing LEAD TIME, already translated:
              "Ready today" / "Ready in 1–2 business days" / "Order in" /
              "Sold out"
      lead  = today | 1-2 | order | out   (machine value of text)

  Owner rule, 2026-11-13 (redesign): customers see the LEAD TIME ONLY.
  Never a count, a bucket ("40+ available"), "Low stock", "Only N left",
  "In stock", a warehouse, a shelf or a supplier name.
    today = our own stock (kind own) AND snippets/pt-supplier-tier.liquid
            returns 'A' - the same rule as the same-day booking floor.
    1-2   = own stock that is Tier B, or any supplier stock, or untracked.
    order = available but tracked with nothing on hand (continue-selling).
            Wheels never say "Order in" (owner default 2026-11-13: sold-out
            wheels say "Sold out" + call); a wheel in this state says 1-2.
    out   = not available.
  The bucket / low / call thresholds below still decide the internal state
  (call = the page swaps book / add-to-cart for a call link), but no longer
  change what the customer reads. Rendering for pages: snippets/pt-lead-time.liquid.

  Owner rules, 2026-11-10 (state logic; the WORDING part is replaced by the
  2026-11-13 lead-time rule above):
  - Only OUR physical stock may say "In stock": 42 Ave (109466288403),
    Edmonton Trail (113250304275) and Warehouse Inventory (75571462419).
    Supplier stock (Trail Tire, ATW, R. Thibert, NCT, DT) says
    "Available to order" — never "In stock".
  - Quantity is shown as a bucket, never an exact number:
      >= 40 "40+ available", >= 16 "16+", >= 12 "12+", 9-11 "8+",
      <= 8 "Low stock — call to book" (no number; the page swaps the
      book / add-to-cart buttons for a call link).
    Every threshold is a theme setting (Theme settings > Stock wording).
    "Low stock" (bookable, no number) only appears if the owner sets the
    call-to-book threshold BELOW the low-stock threshold (e.g. 3 vs 8).
  - Own stock counted in the last 30 days (product tag, default Counted30)
    shows the exact number ONLY when it is small (at or below the low-stock
    threshold, default 8): "4 in stock", and call-to-book does not apply,
    because the count is known to be right. Above that it gets the same
    bucket as everything else ("In stock · 40+ available"). Owner
    2026-11-15: a counted tire showed "191 in stock" - big counts are never
    shown exactly.

  How "own stock" is detected (first match wins, all per variant):
   1. App metafield variant.metafields.pt.own_qty (number_integer) = units
      on hand at 42 Ave + Edmonton Trail + Warehouse Inventory. When it is
      present it is the count we show for own stock. NOT written by the app
      yet. Contract: owner = princetires-app own-stock sync (the same tick
      that pushes 42 Ave / Edmonton Trail / Warehouse levels to Shopify);
      metafieldsSet on the VARIANT, namespace "pt", key "own_qty", type
      number_integer, value = sum of "available" at those three locations,
      write an explicit 0 when it runs out (never delete — deleting falls
      back to rules 2 and 3). Missing metafield = rules 2 and 3 only.
   2. Shopify local pickup: a pickup-enabled location (only the two shops)
      has the variant available, AND the variant is tracked, sells only
      what it has (inventory_policy 'deny'), has quantity > 0, and the
      product is not a supplier listing (tags 'Supplier Stock' or
      'Trail Tire Supply'). StoreAvailability.available alone is NOT proof
      of shelf stock: Shopify also sets it for untracked or continue-selling
      variants and for stock that can be transferred in (warehouse-only
      items come back true at both shops). Real time, no app writes.
      Limit (until pt.own_qty exists): the count for a rule-2 product is
      the variant total over ALL locations. Supplier listings are excluded
      above because DT/NCT stock may be added to Trail Tire / ATW listings;
      if supplier stock were ever put on an untagged own product, its
      bucket would include that supplier stock.
   3. Own-product tag 'Prince Stock' (or legacy 'Prince Tires') and NOT
      'Supplier Stock', tracked and quantity > 0. Covers Warehouse
      Inventory today: measured 2026-11-10, all 108 active variants with
      warehouse-only stock carry 'Prince Stock', and 0 of 384 Prince Stock
      products hold any supplier-location stock (owner rule: supplier
      stock is never added to own products).
   Anything else that is available = supplier stock. Unknown never becomes
   "In stock", and nothing with no on-hand count (untracked, or quantity
   <= 0 while continue-selling) ever says "In stock": it says "Available
   to order" with kind = supplier.

  @param {product} product - The product
  @param {variant} [variant] - Defaults to product.selected_or_first_available_variant.
    store_availabilities is only filled in for that variant, so pass another
    variant only when it is the selected one.
  @param {boolean} [is_wheel] - Pass the page's own wheel test when it has one.
    Omitted = the shared wheel test (no tire size AND bolt pattern, or a
    wheel / rims / alloy type, or tag Wheels, or a blank type whose title
    names a wheel / rim). Only used to keep wheels off "Order in".

  @example
    {%- capture pt_stock -%}{% render 'pt-stock-state', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign pt_stock = pt_stock | strip | split: '|' -%}
    kind = pt_stock[0], state = pt_stock[1], text = pt_stock[2], lead = pt_stock[3]
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign v = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  # stock_bucket_1..3 (the old "N+ available" buckets) are no longer read:
  # customers see lead time only (2026-11-13). The settings stay in the
  # schema so nothing else breaks.
  assign low_max = settings.stock_low_max | default: 8 | plus: 0
  assign call_max = settings.stock_call_max | default: 8 | plus: 0
  assign counted_tag = settings.stock_counted_tag | default: 'Counted30' | strip

  assign kind = 'out'
  assign state = 'out'
  assign lead = 'out'
  assign label = 'products.stock.lead_out' | t

  if v != blank and v.available
    assign tracked = false
    if v.inventory_management == 'shopify'
      assign tracked = true
    endif
    assign qty = v.inventory_quantity | default: 0 | plus: 0

    assign is_supplier_tag = false
    if product.tags contains 'Supplier Stock'
      assign is_supplier_tag = true
    endif

    assign is_own = false
    assign own_qty = -1

    # Rule 1: app metafield (authoritative count when present).
    assign own_mf = v.metafields.pt.own_qty.value
    assign has_mf = false
    if own_mf != blank
      assign has_mf = true
      assign own_mf = own_mf | plus: 0
      if own_mf > 0
        assign is_own = true
        assign own_qty = own_mf
      endif
    endif

    # Rule 2: real-time local pickup at one of our two shops. Only counts
    # with a real on-hand count (tracked, deny, qty > 0) on a listing that
    # is not a supplier listing - see the header for why.
    assign is_supplier_listing = is_supplier_tag
    if product.tags contains 'Trail Tire Supply'
      assign is_supplier_listing = true
    endif
    if has_mf == false and is_supplier_listing == false and tracked and v.inventory_policy == 'deny' and qty > 0
      assign pickup_now = v.store_availabilities | where: 'pick_up_enabled', true | where: 'available', true
      if pickup_now.size > 0
        assign is_own = true
        assign own_qty = qty
      endif
    endif

    # Rule 3: own-product tag (covers Warehouse Inventory today).
    if has_mf == false and is_supplier_tag == false and tracked and qty > 0
      if product.tags contains 'Prince Stock' or product.tags contains 'Prince Tires'
        assign is_own = true
        assign own_qty = qty
      endif
    endif

    assign kind = 'supplier'
    if is_own
      assign kind = 'own'
    endif

    assign is_counted = false
    if is_own and own_qty > 0 and counted_tag != blank and product.tags contains counted_tag
      assign is_counted = true
    endif

    assign n = qty
    if is_own and own_qty > 0
      assign n = own_qty
    endif

    # Internal state only (see header). The thresholds no longer reach the
    # customer: they only decide call-to-book and what staff tooling reads.
    # Live 2026-11-15: a big counted number is never treated as exact.
    if is_counted and own_qty <= low_max
      assign state = 'exact'
    elsif tracked == false or qty <= 0
      # Untracked or continue-selling with nothing on hand: nothing proves
      # it is on our shelf, so it is never own stock.
      assign kind = 'supplier'
      assign state = 'plain'
    elsif n <= call_max
      assign state = 'call'
    elsif n <= low_max
      assign state = 'low'
    else
      assign state = 'bucket'
    endif

    # Lead time - the only thing the customer reads.
    if kind == 'own'
      capture lt_tier
        render 'pt-supplier-tier', product: product
      endcapture
      assign lt_tier = lt_tier | strip
      if lt_tier == 'A'
        assign lead = 'today'
      else
        assign lead = '1-2'
      endif
    elsif tracked and qty <= 0
      assign lead = 'order'
    else
      assign lead = '1-2'
    endif

    if lead == 'order'
      # Wheels never say "Order in" (owner default, 2026-11-13).
      assign lt_wheel = is_wheel
      if lt_wheel == nil
        assign lt_wheel = false
        assign lt_ts = product.metafields.custom.tire_size | default: ''
        if lt_ts == blank
          if product.metafields.custom.bolt_pattern != blank
            assign lt_wheel = true
          endif
          assign lt_type = product.type | downcase
          if lt_type contains 'accessor'
            assign lt_type = 'tire'
          endif
          unless lt_type contains 'tire'
            if lt_type contains 'wheel' or lt_type contains 'rims' or lt_type contains 'alloy' or product.tags contains 'Wheels'
              assign lt_wheel = true
            elsif lt_type == blank
              assign lt_title = product.title | downcase
              unless lt_title contains 'tire'
                if lt_title contains 'wheel' or lt_title contains ' rim'
                  assign lt_wheel = true
                endif
              endunless
            endif
          endunless
        endif
      endif
      if lt_wheel == true or lt_wheel == 'true'
        assign lead = '1-2'
      endif
    endif

    case lead
      when 'today'
        assign label = 'products.stock.lead_today' | t
      when 'order'
        assign label = 'products.stock.lead_order' | t
      else
        assign label = 'products.stock.lead_days' | t
    endcase
  endif

  echo kind | append: '|' | append: state | append: '|' | append: label | append: '|' | append: lead
-%}
